{"tool_name":"morpholibj","contents":["neubias","oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"morpholibj","home":"http://ijpb.github.io/MorphoLibJ/","summary":"Library that proposes a large collection of generic tools based on mathematical morphology to process binary and grey-level 2D and 3D images, integrated into user-friendly plugins.","addition_date":"2017-08-03T18:51:49Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:50Z","tool_type":["Plug-in"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:morpholibj","credit":[{"email":"Philippe.Andrey@versailles.inra.fr","name":"Philippe Andrey","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www-ijpb.versailles.inra.fr/en/bc/equipes/modelisation-imagerie/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://imagej.net/MorphoLibJ"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Filtering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3695"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Image analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3443"}]}],"name":"MorphoLibJ","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2016 The Author Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.Motivation: Mathematical morphology (MM) provides many powerful operators for processing 2D and 3D images. However, most MM plugins currently implemented for the popular ImageJ/Fiji platform are limited to the processing of 2D images. Results: The MorphoLibJ library proposes a large collection of generic tools based on MM to process binary and grey-level 2D and 3D images, integrated into user-friendly plugins. We illustrate how MorphoLibJ can facilitate the exploitation of 3D images of plant tissues.","authors":[{"name":"Andrey P."},{"name":"Arganda-Carreras I."},{"name":"Legland D."}],"citationCount":323,"date":"2016-11-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"MorphoLibJ: Integrated library and plugins for mathematical morphology with ImageJ"},"pmid":"27412086"}],"topic":[{"term":"Imaging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3382"},{"term":"Mathematics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3315"}],"validated":1},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:morpholibj/plugin/ijpb.github.io","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":false,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":548,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"-1"},{"count":6,"year":"2017"},{"count":14,"year":"2018"},{"count":33,"year":"2019"},{"count":52,"year":"2020"},{"count":58,"year":"2026"},{"count":72,"year":"2021"},{"count":72,"year":"2025"},{"count":75,"year":"2024"},{"count":80,"year":"2022"},{"count":85,"year":"2023"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw413","pmid":"27412086","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"MorphoLibJ: integrated library and plugins for mathematical morphology with ImageJ.","year":2016}]}],"readme":true,"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":200,"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"email":true,"issue_tracking":{"public_tracker":true,"resolve_time":"PT11042891S"}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/morpholibj","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":null,"@type":"metrics","distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":false,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[],"readme":true,"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":200,"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"issue_tracking":{"public_tracker":true,"resolve_time":"PT11042891S"}}}]},"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>MorphoLibJ is a library of plugin for ImageJ with functionalities for image processing such as filtering, reconstructing, segmenting, etc... Tools are based on Mathematical morphology with more rigorous mathematical approach than in the standard tools of ImageJ in particular for surface (or perimeter) measurements which are usually based on voxel counting.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"http://imagej.net/MorphoLibJ#Measurements\">http://imagej.net/MorphoLibJ#Measurements</a></p>\n\n<p>Among the features:</p>\n\n<p>Morphological operations :&nbsp;&nbsp;Dilation, Erosion,&nbsp;Opening,&nbsp;&nbsp;Closing , Top hat (white and black), Morphological gradient (aka Beucher Gradient), Morphological&nbsp;Laplacian, Morphological reconstruction, Maxima/Minima , Extended Maxima/Minima -Watershed (classic or controlled) -Image overlay -Image labelling -Geodesic diameter -Region Adjacency Graph -Granulometry curves, morphological image analysis.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","summary":"","value":"<p>MorphoLibJ is a library of plugin for ImageJ with functionalities for image processing such as filtering, reconstructing, segmenting, etc... Tools are based on Mathematical morphology with more rigorous mathematical approach than in the standard tools of ImageJ in particular for surface (or perimeter) measurements which are usually based on voxel counting.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"http://imagej.net/MorphoLibJ#Measurements\">http://imagej.net/MorphoLibJ#Measurements</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Among the features:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Morphological operations :&nbsp;&nbsp;Dilation, Erosion,&nbsp;Opening,&nbsp;&nbsp;Closing , Top hat (white and black), Morphological gradient (aka Beucher Gradient), Morphological&nbsp;Laplacian, Morphological reconstruction, Maxima/Minima , Extended Maxima/Minima -Watershed (classic or controlled) -Image overlay -Image labelling -Geodesic diameter -Region Adjacency Graph -Granulometry curves, morphological image analysis.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2023-04-25T17:17:43+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2016-10-01T16:31:47+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":374,"comment_count":1,"last_comment_name":"","last_comment_timestamp":1523443269,"last_comment_uid":2800,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"Legland, David"},{"value":"Arganda-Carreras, Ignacio"}],"has_biological_terms":[],"has_comparison":[],"has_documentation":[{"options":[],"title":"MorphoLibJ user manual (v1.3.3)","uri":"https://github.com/ijpb/MorphoLibJ/releases/download/v1.3.3/MorphoLibJ-manual-v1.3.3.pdf"}],"has_doi":[],"has_entry_curator":[{"target_id":175,"target_type":"user","target_uuid":"3750f9fc-5ff9-4411-8990-b3e992f13b8d","url":"/user/175"}],"has_function":[{"target_id":4004,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation_Image_segmentation","url":"/image-segmentation"},{"target_id":4083,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation_Cell_segmentation","url":"/cell-segmentation"},{"target_id":4159,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation_Watershed","url":"/watershed-segmentation-0"},{"target_id":4058,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation_Cell_counting","url":"/object-counting"},{"target_id":4074,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation_Feature_extraction","url":"/object-feature-extraction"},{"target_id":4007,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation_Shape_features","url":"/shape-features"},{"target_id":4168,